<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John of Gischala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/66">66</a>–<a href="/years/70">70</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as John ben Levi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John of Gischala was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war">First Jewish–Roman War</a> from the town of Gischala in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a>. After Vespasian took Galilee he escaped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, where he joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zealots">Zealots</a> and fought rival factions under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bar-giora">Simon bar Giora</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleazar-ben-simon">Eleazar ben Simon</a>. He was captured when the city fell in 70 CE and sentenced to life imprisonment.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Jerusalem then split between rival factions under <b>John of Gischala</b>, Simon bar Giora and Eleazar ben Simon, who fought each other and burned food stores.</blockquote><a href="/state/provisional-government-of-judea">Provisional Government of Judea</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Ancient sites in Gush Halav, in what is now <a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=33.03,35.45&amp;year=68" aria-label="Ancient sites in Gush Halav on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5458 964 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of John of Gischala"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5908 1234h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5908 1234h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=33.03,35.45&amp;year=68">What was here in 68 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
